-- Two independent perspectives, followed by one synthesizer.
-- Uses the installed native DSCO swarm tool; this performs real inference.
-- Run with DSCO_AUTO_GOAL=0 DSCO_TOOL_CHOICE=none for one-response workers.
local l = require("lingo")
local dsco = require("lingo.dsco")
local swarm = dsco.tool("swarm")
local model = args.model or "gpt-5.6-luna"
local provider = args.provider or "openai-codex"

local brief = [[
Distributed Systems is developing Lingo: a language for expressing worlds.
GraphSub stores shared world artifacts; DSCO is the operator; Autobot executes
work; Chimera routes inference. The user wants higher abstractions: worlds,
perspectives, possibilities, intentions, patterns and organizations.

Current executable Lingo uses Lua 5.1 on LuaJIT. The actual API includes:
local l=require("lingo"); local w=l.world{id="studio"}
w:define("Class", {field=l.stored("string"),
  answer=l.derived("boolean", function(self) return self.field~="" end)})
w:new("Class", "id", {field="value"}); w:ref("id").answer
Types include boolean, string, integer, json, l.types.ref("Class"),
l.types.list(type). w:scenario(name, callback) provides temporary assumptions;
w:override(object,field,value) applies inside that callback. Baseline is restored.
w:why(object,field) exposes read dependencies. Calculated values and scenarios
cannot execute tools. require("lingo.dsco").tool("swarm"):json{...} explicitly
calls the real host swarm tool. Stored-world snapshots retain data and pinned
definitions; they do not resume processes. Pattern, organization, intention,
world:imagine, and durable goal-instance APIs remain DESIGN PROPOSALS.

Task: design one compelling research-studio world in which two perspectives
produce contributions and a synthesis makes their agreement and disagreement
inspectable. Make the abstraction understandable to a programmer. No metaphysical
claims. Do not claim proposed APIs exist. Work only from this supplied brief.
Do not call tools, browse, spawn, or edit files. Return the requested answer now.
]]

local receipt = swarm:call {
    action="map_reduce",
    name="lingo-world-studio",
    model=model,
    tasks={
        {provider=provider, model=model, effort="low", task=brief .. [[
ROLE: ARCHITECT. In at most 300 words propose the domain objects and relationships,
one meaningful calculated question, and one useful possible world. Include a tiny
Lua-style example; clearly label any proposed convenience syntax.]]},
        {provider=provider, model=model, effort="low", task=brief .. [[
ROLE: SKEPTIC. In at most 300 words identify the three most consequential semantic
mistakes this design could make and give concrete rules that avoid them. Explain
how dissent remains visible and what would count as evidence for a conclusion.]]},
    },
    coordinator=brief .. [[
ROLE: SYNTHESIZER. You receive the architect and skeptic outputs below. Produce a
single useful Markdown proposal of at most 550 words. Start with the research
world's purpose; define its objects and one calculated question; include one small
example using current Lingo syntax if the supplied API suffices. Reconcile the
perspectives explicitly, preserve a consequential disagreement, and distinguish
working primitives from proposed extensions. End with one concrete operator
interaction. Treat every worker statement as a proposal to evaluate, not proof.]],
    coordinator_provider=provider,
    coordinator_model=model,
    coordinator_effort="low",
    max_worker_turns=1,
    max_coordinator_turns=1,
    timeout=90,
    map_total_timeout=90,
    reduce_timeout=90,
    op_total_timeout=180,
    max_concurrency=2,
    strict_success_count=true,
    map_refill_rounds=0,
    coordinator_fallback=false,
    preserve_on_timeout=false,
    budget=0.25,
}

-- Retain execution evidence even when a phase did not complete.
local decoded, result = l.try(function() return l.decode(receipt.result) end)
if not decoded then result = {error=receipt.result} end
local status
if type(result.group_id) == "number" then
    status = swarm:call {action="status", group_id=result.group_id}
end
return {purpose="Express a research studio as a world",
    roles={"architect", "skeptic", "synthesizer"},
    succeeded=receipt.ok and result.complete == true and result.degraded == false,
    run=result, execution=status, receipt=receipt}
